Geant4 — nuclear-structure, EM and HI-XS production data
================================================================================
This product includes data developed by Members of the Geant4 Collaboration
(http://cern.ch/geant4), reformatted to Parquet by eXoma. The Geant4 name is not
used to endorse or promote nucl-parquet, and the Geant4 Collaboration does not
endorse this product. No Geant4 source or binary is included in this
distribution; only computed output and reformatted data tables.

Affected tables include the ENSDF-derived structure and decay tables
(data/meta/ensdf, decay, decay_detailed), the electron bremsstrahlung and
electron-stopping tables (data/em/electron_brem*, data/stopping/em,
data/stopping/ESTAR.parquet), and the heavy-ion production cross-sections
(hi-xs-prod).

================================================================================
catima — used to compute heavy-ion stopping power (catima_*.parquet)
================================================================================
Stopping-power values were computed with catima (A. Prochazka), based on ATIMA
(GSI). Only the computed Parquet output is redistributed. catima's source and
binaries are AGPL-3.0 and are NOT included in this distribution, and pycatima is
NOT a runtime dependency of the nucl-parquet distribution — it is required only
to regenerate the shards.

